From 751ad6d9e1b76d3ac86834bd92654eba4f670294 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yaegerbomb42 <yaeger.james42@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:40:50 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] feat(vm): interactive terminal shell to the VM (t32)

Adds POST /api/runtime/vm/exec, which lets a user type a command
into their computer and streams the output onto the telemetry bus
under a dedicated "shell" run.

- lib/vm/argv: POSIX-like tokenizer (quotes/escapes) for shell
  lines, plus a shellCommandText rejoin; hard limits on arg count,
  arg length, and command length.
- app/api/runtime/vm/exec: normalizes cmd (string or argv array),
  validates, applies the harness risk classifier (deny/ask never
  run from the terminal), and starts the shell run via VmManager
  in argv form.
- lib/runtime/manager: execShell/executeShell stream shell.cmd,
  shell.output, vm.starting/ready, run.finished/error events, and
  track shell runs alongside agent runs (list/ownsRun/resetVm).
- ComputerScreen: terminal view gets a live input line with command
  history (Up/Down, persisted in localStorage) and streams its own
  shell session independently of the agent run.
- Tests for the route (auth, validation, risk gate, argv execution,
  failure streaming) and for the tokenizer.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
